+# HBNF Skins cold-reopen data preservation — review-only candidate
+
+**Source basis:** Exact deployed public 44-asset HBNF Worker package `16ILHuKGKxbll0kpagHS5UFu3xtxUttZz` (3,264,714 bytes; SHA-256 `29d3c6c2aa9038063c659a5361b932ce2c9819a481fd020b5172701450dc477a`); recovered source commit `376b31ccf3be3fed06cb7a17810e7ad15ca0cb01` from independently verified Drive Git bundle `1GRWDuh1JWWXuQEtzQDaTHrbfawVCu-A9` (SHA-256 `cc6969cd2d96bd3e0af5997c0fcfd099f6786f639b8404c8bb52571855fd7c21`). Independent source/package readback: 44/44 files identical before modification.
+
+**Scope:** Only `public/skins.html` changes in the 44-file live candidate. Adds a recoverable write-ahead pending draft for Skins, protects unfinished edits on cold app reopen, quarantines scoreful legacy cache when cloud lacks it, performs independent server GET after CAS UPDATE before saying saved and clearing the marker, surfaces pending/failed/conflict alerts outside the collapsed tools menu. No fixtures/scores/tags are sent to production. No changes to Glow, Cart, CSS files, index page, Worker bindings or database schema.
+
+**Verification as of Oct 29:** 11 isolated Node VM source-path tests pass (cold reopen, offline, conflict, CAS zero-row, ACK without readback, two consecutive saves, marker quota failure, legacy cache preservation, repeated reopen, unrelated Back/Tags preservation). Inline scripts pass Node syntax checks, and Chromium-rendered responsive screenshots at 390×844, 430×932, and 768×1024 show the alert without document-wide horizontal overflow. Screenshots are **not** real iPhone or Supabase integration acceptance. No production API writes; no production deployment.
+
+**Remaining gates:** Native local Supabase/PostgREST + real Chromium integration on production-equivalent fixture; regressions for multiple concurrent clients, stale reads and cross-week data, Realtime races, quota failure, offline/reconnect, actual physical iPhone app; independently verified active Worker identity; two-phase same-manifest release admission, exact candidate and current rollback downloaded-back; authorized deployment, 44-route readback, durable closeout; one consolidated real owner-device acceptance. Until then this candidate is REVIEW_ONLY and must not be installed or called fixed. Never infer real Oct 27 winners from simulated tests or apply test fixtures to production.
+
+**Known limitation:** This deliberately does not auto-reconcile conflicting cloud/client data. The local draft is kept and a conflict is shown; resolving actual scores requires independently verified owner evidence. This is safer than silently overwriting either version.
